WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.980
Yemen is in the midst of a civil war but

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:06.990
 

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:08.629
it really depends from which perspective

00:00:08.629 --> 00:00:08.639
 

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:10.370
you're looking at it to say what war is

00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:10.380
 

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:12.620
being fought. The outcome of the conflict

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:12.630
 

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.539
in Yemen has direct ramifications for

00:00:14.539 --> 00:00:14.549
 

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:16.099
the future of the Middle East region

00:00:16.099 --> 00:00:16.109
 

00:00:16.109 --> 00:00:18.050
because of how it's played into the

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:18.060
 

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.540
sectarian dynamics in the region and the

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:20.550
 

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.849
actual power conflict between Saudi

00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:22.859
 

00:00:22.859 --> 00:00:24.859
Arabia and Iran that is taken root

00:00:24.859 --> 00:00:24.869
 

00:00:24.869 --> 00:00:26.720
inside of Yemen. There are now two

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:26.730
 

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.820
governments inside of Yemen both seen as

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:28.830
 

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:31.490
legitimate by their followers. What we're

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:31.500
 

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.830
looking at is a situation where Saudi

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:33.840
 

00:00:33.840 --> 00:00:36.110
Arabia is backing a southern government

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:36.120
 

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.479
that's based in Aden and recognized by

00:00:38.479 --> 00:00:38.489
 

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:40.580
the international community and Iran has

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:40.590
 

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:42.020
back the northern government in Sana'a

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:42.030
 

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:43.910
under the Aahuthi Sallah regime.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:43.920
 

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:46.190
It creates an interesting dynamic where

00:00:46.190 --> 00:00:46.200
 

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:48.410
should the country fracture into two, there

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:48.420
 

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.110
would be an Iranian mini-state and Saudi

00:00:51.110 --> 00:00:51.120
 

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.750
southern border and a Saudi client in

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:53.760
 

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:56.060
the south of Yemen.  This is a significant

00:00:56.060 --> 00:00:56.070
 

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.799
inflection from how Yemen used to be,

00:00:57.799 --> 00:00:57.809
 

00:00:57.809 --> 00:00:59.779
where the entire country used to be

00:00:59.779 --> 00:00:59.789
 

00:00:59.789 --> 00:01:02.420
under Saudi Arabia's influence and the

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:02.430
 

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.310
growing presence of Iran in the region

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:04.320
 

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.390
is a concern.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:05.890
 

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:09.020
How do you think the war in Yemen

00:01:09.020 --> 00:01:09.030
 

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:10.700
effects Middle East dynamics?

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:10.710
 

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.140
Let us know in the comments section and

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:12.150
 

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.399
let us know what other topics you want

00:01:13.399 --> 00:01:13.409
 

00:01:13.409 --> 00:01:20.450
AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

